WEBVTT

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:07.980
Narumi.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:12.160
The first place I went
to find out who I am...

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:17.660
was the apartment I used to live in
with my mom.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:25.840
I'm home!

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:30.170
Mom, I got another perfect score
on a test...

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:36.220
Mom...?

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.680
Let it bloom or let it wither

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:42.600
The setting sun ignites the horizon

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:47.230
And the gears turn

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.120
When the horn blows, the flames dance

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:03.000
The story waits for no-one

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:05.880
Off they go, the gears are churning

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:09.130
A red past chases after you

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.460
The jester's smile

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:14.340
What's behind the mask?

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:17.180
You can't erase the scars

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:19.930
No matter how they burn

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.060
Let it bloom or let it wither

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:25.980
The setting sun ignites the horizon

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:31.780
Alone in the depths of the night

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:35.820
Let out a cry that can cut through fate

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:38.370
That's the cue to begin

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:41.870
The curtain is rising, it's time to dance

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:46.040
Everybody sheds tears at the end

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:49.130
So hold them in now and keep going

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:53.760
Until the day the curtain falls

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:59.100
The gears will keep turning

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:09.310
"IN MOURNING"

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:11.770
#15 Back to the starting point

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:16.530
Mom was a mistress,
so I was the only one at her funeral.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:31.960
A lawyer appeared and took me away.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:39.640
That was when I first met Dad.

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:43.680
But you know what, Narumi?

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.640
I just can't remember.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:50.690
I'm glad you came, Masaru.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.650
I can't remember...

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.200
Dad's face.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:02.070
Are you in good health?

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:06.080
What sports do you not like?
What are your favorite foods?

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:12.130
I began to live with Dad.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.590
But nobody wanted an illegitimate child.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:23.550
I cried all the time back then.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:28.390
Now, now. Boys shouldn't cry like that.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:30.940
Who is it?

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:37.320
I'm Shoji Saiga, your grandpa.

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:39.400
At least, from now on I am.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.580
It's huge!

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.630
There!

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.090
Faster, faster.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:58.090
This is amazing, Grandpa.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:03.640
For some reason, all Saiga men
develop a keen interest in these.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:08.310
Masaru, listen well to
what I have to tell you.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:14.440
If your dad should die before you grow up
and strange things begin to happen...

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:18.940
take that case and run away.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:23.610
Shirogane will protect you.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.490
Oh, wait!

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:32.080
It was just as Grandpa said
before he died.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:38.670
After Dad died in the accident and
everyone found out I inherited everything,

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.840
I was pushed into traffic.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.430
And things fell from above.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:53.850
It wasn't long after,

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.810
that I met Shirogane and you, Narumi.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:00.030
And everything began to happen.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:02.530
Stop, please!

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:12.830
"KARUIZAWA"

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:17.630
This is where it all started.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:21.010
The Karakuri mansion
that used to be Dad's.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:25.220
I learned a lot of things here
from you Narumi,

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:27.010
and became who I am today.

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:31.680
But it's all gone.

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:41.320
Narumi.

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:43.320
You, boy.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:45.700
What are you doing?

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.790
Sorry, I scared you huh?

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.620
I'm the caretaker here.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:59.090
Not that there's much left
after the fire.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:01.590
Geez.

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:05.420
Then why do you still work here?

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:10.850
Well, the late Mr. Saiga
already paid me to.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:12.720
So, who are you?

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:14.730
I... I'm...

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:17.100
the adopted son.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:19.810
What!

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:23.110
Tell me your name!

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:27.110
It's Masaru. Masaru Saiga.

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:31.620
Come with me.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:38.000
To think you'd actually come.

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:40.170
Um, what's going on?

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:43.880
It was about 30 years ago, I think.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:50.220
Your late father asked me
a peculiar favor.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:53.720
He said a boy named Masaru
would come here.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:57.980
And I must give him this.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.150
30 years ago?

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:05.780
Wait a minute.

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:10.820
But I came here by coincidence,
by my own free will.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:14.450
How did Dad know...?

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:18.460
There's a letter, too.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.090
To the current Masaru.

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:31.640
If you are reading this,

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:36.470
it means there was a glitch
in the memory transfer.

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:38.730
Go back to the room.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:40.980
Here is the symbol.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:48.990
What does he mean, memory transfer?

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:51.160
What glitch?

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:54.890
In case the memory transfer
could not be completed...

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:58.930
I am leaving this room intact.

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:00.930
Dad's voice.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:07.650
You came here. That means
you want to know more about yourself.

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:11.650
Why are you in this situation?

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:17.990
Why did your father leave his fortune
to an adopted son?

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:20.040
That's right.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:23.910
The brain scan and download were initiated

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:29.960
from the outermost layer of brain cells,
but must have gone wrong at some point.

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:34.170
An imperfect regeneration such as this
was always a possibility.

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:37.180
What are you talking about?

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:42.980
So I'm leaving this voice recording
to stimulate your memory.

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:45.640
I don't get it.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:50.570
You are not Masaru Saiga.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:57.410
It's true that you once were.

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:03.500
But now, you're a different person with
the memory and personality of another.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.040
Wait...

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:09.170
Dad...?

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:14.010
All information in the brain
can be converted to electrical impulses

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:16.380
and downloaded to another brain.

00:10:16.930 --> 00:10:22.010
So I am speaking not to Masaru Saiga,
but to myself.

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:25.180
I didn't leave everything to Masaru.

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:30.360
I left it to myself, Sadayoshi Saiga.

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:34.360
Yes, he said his name was Masaru.

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:37.860
I think he headed for the mansion.

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:42.450
Sadayoshi Saiga has become Masaru Saiga.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:47.120
It's all part of a larger plan
with a single aim.

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.960
They're all mine.

00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:00.680
But I'm me, Dad.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:02.930
I don't have your memory.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:07.730
To stimulate the complete restoration
of my memory

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:10.560
I will explain the download process.

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:17.650
Above one chair is a scanner to extract
the information from my brain.

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:23.450
Next to the other is a computer with
programs based on my daily activities.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:30.120
Both sets of data are downloaded into
a bio-chip implanted in your brain.

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:34.590
And then the "you" that is "me"
is complete.

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:36.880
You are me.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:40.630
You're lying.

00:11:42.140 --> 00:11:45.600
It's not true, I won't believe it!

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:51.600
Oh yes, I will leave some marionettes
just in case.

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:55.190
They're much better
than the old Saiga marionettes.

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:58.110
Much more useful.

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:03.280
You mean...

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:07.490
You took me in after Mom died...

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:10.330
And left me your fortune...

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:15.840
And cared for my health
when we first met...

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:20.090
all so you could use my body?

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:23.180
Current Masaru.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:27.850
You have grown strong. You are smart, too.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:30.060
I'm proud of you.

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:35.610
Now remember. You are Sadayoshi Saiga.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:45.620
Remember.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:57.630
Who am I?

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:03.800
What...?

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:08.140
What a transformation you've undergone,
Sadayoshi Saiga.

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:10.310
Wait...

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:15.270
If you ever survived
and acquired Masaru Saiga's body,

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:17.270
we were told you'd come here.

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:20.030
It's just as Master Shoji said.

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:22.570
Master Shoji? You mean Grandpa?

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:24.360
Who are you?

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.120
You're good at acting like a kid.

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:33.040
But we know that you downloaded
your brain into that child.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:36.210
This is going to be your grave.

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:43.510
You mean, you're...

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:46.680
Yeah, we're puppeteers of Kuroga Village.

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:51.810
We owe much to Master Shoji.
And so we will kill you for him!

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:55.810
No, I'm...

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:57.150
I don't want to hear it!

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:09.870
I will leave some marionettes
just in case.

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:15.500
They're much better
than the old Saiga marionettes.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:25.630
It won't open. Why?

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:30.600
Open up, please!

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:32.930
What are you doing, Master Sadayoshi!

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:36.180
The finger holes by the keyhole
are open now.

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:38.770
Put your fingers in them, remember?

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:39.900
Who said that?

00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:45.280
You can't escape now.

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:49.620
Hurry up and put your fingers in them!

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:54.750
Be prepared. I'm going to crush you!

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:06.170
He can move it?

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:09.590
Fight back!

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:15.850
It's heavy...

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:21.650
You have to pull with all your strength
to move Goyellemes.

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:34.280
He beat Shogetsu?

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:40.420
So this is the puppet
Sadayoshi built by himself for himself.

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:42.210
Damn it.

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:46.460
Phew, you did it Master Sadayoshi.

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:49.510
Where's that voice coming from?

00:15:55.060 --> 00:15:58.020
I'm Gryphon. You made me.

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:04.480
If an error occurred, you might have
problems recovering your memory.

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:06.900
I'm here to help.

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:10.650
Gryphon?

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:12.410
Are you okay?

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:14.990
Sorry, I let him get a marionette.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:19.290
But now we have proof that he's Sadayoshi.

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:23.500
You're right. No regular kid
could control a puppet.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:27.130
I guess Goyellemes is too heavy.

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:30.920
Here they come!
Gotta get a different puppet.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:45.060
How about it?
Captain Nemo is a lot lighter, eh?

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:47.270
Yeah, but it's so wobbly.

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:51.780
Make a circle with the right middle finger
and draw it into your left palm.

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:03.040
-Impossible!
-Let's get out of here.

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:09.300
Well, well.

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:14.300
Seems like your memory
hasn't revived at all, Master Sadayoshi.

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:16.510
Um...

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:20.560
Oh yeah. I have to chase them.
There's so much I have to ask.

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:24.310
What Dad was. Why they're after him.

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:27.060
You got a ride right over there.

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:30.400
There's another puppet, remember?

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:36.740
What is this?

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:39.740
The finger holes are behind his head.

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:49.000
Jump on!

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:55.590
Hang on tight.

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:11.650
Really? He's awake?

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:14.240
Yes, it's been 9 months.

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:17.070
How is he?

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:19.950
Don't worry, he's stable.

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:23.120
Sorry for worrying you,
people of Kuroga.

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:26.000
Not at all.

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:28.830
We are greatly in your debt.

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:33.420
We will do anything for you.

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:36.680
Where is Sadayoshi?

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:40.800
The man who was my son
by social standards.

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:42.760
Has he died?

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:49.100
We got a report today that a boy appeared
at the Karuizawa villa.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:52.190
He said his name was Masaru Saiga.

00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:54.780
Are you positive it's him?

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:58.780
We've sent some experienced puppeteers
to confirm it.

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:05.370
But no regular boy would have any business
going there anyway.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:07.790
Which means...

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:10.080
What a catastrophe!

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:13.840
You mean he survived?

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:16.670
And now...

00:19:17.220 --> 00:19:22.180
he has downloaded his brain into Masaru.

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:25.970
Poor Masaru...

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:29.900
I'm sorry Grandpa couldn't protect you.

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:34.230
Village chief, may I ask you a favor?

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:39.240
There is something I must ask that man.

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:49.870
We don't want to guide him to our village.
Let's change routes.

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:54.710
No, keep going.
I just got a call from the chief.

00:19:55.050 --> 00:19:58.720
Master Shoji has awakened
and wants Sadayoshi brought to him.

00:20:02.390 --> 00:20:03.220
Like this, maybe?

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:06.850
What precarious piloting,
Master Sadayoshi!

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:10.600
Don't talk to me now,
I'm doing the best I can.

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:14.650
Besides, I'm not Sadayoshi. I'm Masaru.

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:18.240
Yeah, I'm beginning to think so too.

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:21.910
But maybe he just hasn't awakened yet.

00:20:35.090 --> 00:20:37.550
I did it. It's flying, Grandpa.

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:41.630
I told you. The secret is in
the length of the kite tail.

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:49.640
Masaru, don't let it get to you
that you're not a true Saiga child.

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:51.770
Soar high, just like that kite.

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:56.270
You're shying away again.

00:20:57.020 --> 00:21:00.940
Listen well. You must say everything
you wish to say.

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:02.200
There you go.

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:05.200
It's so high!

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:14.580
It's just too sudden.
He was in such good health.

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:17.960
I heard he got lost
trekking in the mountains.

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:23.680
It's him, the mistress's boy.

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:30.350
Lucky him. Once Sadayoshi takes the reins,
he'll be a CEO's son.

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:35.190
Grandpa...

00:21:35.900 --> 00:21:37.980
Grandpa...!

00:21:55.920 --> 00:21:57.170
Grandpa...!

00:21:58.750 --> 00:21:59.630
You're alive!

00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:02.050
Stop right there, Sadayoshi!

00:22:07.140 --> 00:22:08.470
Grandpa?

00:22:27.570 --> 00:22:31.910
Avoiding the crowds,
I walk in the dark

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:36.960
And wait with bated breath in the wings

00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:41.540
My expression is calm
while I scream inside

00:22:41.710 --> 00:22:46.420
On the verge of being torn apart

00:22:46.630 --> 00:22:51.300
I dance and beckon you to join me

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:56.180
As a shadow swings
across the stage

00:22:56.350 --> 00:22:59.190
I tell myself this is
the last time

00:22:59.350 --> 00:23:05.190
But I can't seem to
cut myself free

00:23:05.400 --> 00:23:09.660
Too scared to stop for a moment

00:23:10.120 --> 00:23:15.330
My impatience hides
the cries of somebody left behind

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:23.590
Nobody notices the shadow
standing in the sudden rain

00:23:23.880 --> 00:23:31.680
Somewhere far away,
a memory of you is saying goodbye

00:23:31.850 --> 00:23:39.020
I stand here watching,
no longer able to reach you
